{{PROJECT_DESCRIPTION}} - Type: {{PROJECT_TYPE}}, Stack: {{STACK}}, Docs language: {{DOC_LANGUAGE}}.

## Rules
1. Ask when unsure; never assume requirements, stack or architecture.
2. **Never access the system database** (no queries, DB CLIs, migrations applied, dumps, container exec) and **never read `.env`, credentials, keys or connection strings.** If DB access seems necessary, stop and ask a human. Generate migrations as files only.
3. Work spec-first: requirements -> design -> tasks in `docs/specs/<feature>/`, approved by the user, before code.
4. Strict TDD: failing test -> minimal code -> refactor.
5. Follow Clean Code, Clean Architecture, DDD, SOLID unless the user decided otherwise ({{ENGINEERING_PRINCIPLES}}).
6. Confirm with the user before destructive or outward-facing actions.

